#, no-wrap
msgid "Create and normal-order the Hamiltonian {#create-and-normal-order-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Gumawa at i-normal-order ang Hamiltonian {#create-and-normal-order-the-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the FCIDump data into a fermionic operator and applies normal ordering to simplify the operator structure.\n"
msgstr "Kino-convert ang FCIDump data sa isang fermionic operator at naglalapat ng normal ordering para pasimplehin ang istruktura ng operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group terms by electronic structure {#group-terms-by-electronic-structure}"
msgstr "I-group ang mga term ayon sa electronic structure {#group-terms-by-electronic-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Groups related Hamiltonian terms by electronic structure before constructing their evolution circuits.\n"
msgstr "Ginagrupo ang magkakaugnay na Hamiltonian term ayon sa electronic structure bago buuin ang kanilang evolution circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate sampling weights, then normalize and map to qubit operators {#calculate-sampling-weights-then-normalize-and-map-to-qubit-operators}"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang sampling weights, pagkatapos ay i-normalize at i-map sa qubit operators {#calculate-sampling-weights-then-normalize-and-map-to-qubit-operators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Order matters here.** Normalization rescales every coefficient to unit magnitude *in place*, so the sampling weights must be computed first. If normalization runs first, every $|c_j|$ reads back as exactly `1.0` and each group's weight collapses into a bare count of its terms — the sampling distribution would then be driven by group size rather than by the physical coefficients.\n"
msgstr "**Mahalaga ang pagkakasunod-sunod dito.** Nire-rescale ng normalization ang bawat coefficient sa unit magnitude *in place*, kaya dapat munang kalkulahin ang sampling weights. Kung mauuna ang normalization, ang bawat $|c_j|$ ay babalik bilang eksaktong `1.0` at ang weight ng bawat grupo ay magiging simpleng bilang na lang ng mga term nito — kaya ang sampling distribution ay itutulak ng laki ng grupo sa halip na ng mga pisikal na coefficient.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each group's weight is the **mean** absolute coefficient of its terms. The Python tab's `QDriftTrotterization` pass uses the same weight for a grouped Hamiltonian. Using the sum instead would make $\\lambda$ scale with group size, which in turn skews the evolution time $t_k = \\lambda\\tau/n$.\n"
msgstr "Ang weight ng bawat grupo ay ang **mean** absolute coefficient ng mga term nito. Ginagamit ng `QDriftTrotterization` pass ng Python tab ang parehong weight para sa isang grouped Hamiltonian. Kung sum ang gagamitin, magsa-scale ang $\\lambda$ ayon sa laki ng grupo, na siya namang magbabago sa evolution time na $t_k = \\lambda\\tau/n$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The weight $\\lambda_i = \\frac{1}{|G_i|}\\sum_{j \\in G_i} |c_{ij}|$ is the mean absolute coefficient over the terms of group $G_i$, read from the original coefficients. Normalization then rescales each fermionic term to unit magnitude before the Jordan-Wigner transformation, preserving only its phase/sign in the evolved operator. This matches qDRIFT's normalized-term evolution: coefficient magnitudes determine sampling probabilities via $\\lambda$, while the circuit evolution uses the normalized term so large coefficients are not counted twice.\n"
msgstr "Ang weight na $\\lambda_i = \\frac{1}{|G_i|}\\sum_{j \\in G_i} |c_{ij}|$ ay ang mean absolute coefficient sa mga term ng grupong $G_i$, na binasa mula sa orihinal na mga coefficient. Pagkatapos, nire-rescale ng normalization ang bawat fermionic term sa unit magnitude bago ang Jordan-Wigner transformation, na pinapanatili lang ang phase/sign nito sa na-evolve na operator. Tugma ito sa normalized-term evolution ng qDRIFT: tinutukoy ng laki ng mga coefficient ang sampling probability sa pamamagitan ng $\\lambda$, habang ang circuit evolution ay gumagamit ng normalized na term para hindi mabilang nang dalawang beses ang malalaking coefficient.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample operator sets {#sample-operator-sets}"
msgstr "I-sample ang mga operator set {#sample-operator-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Draws the operator sets for 100 random circuits, each containing 10 groups sampled from the weighted distribution. The next step turns these sets into the ensemble of qDRIFT circuits.\n"
msgstr "Kumukuha ng mga operator set para sa 100 random na circuit, bawat isa ay may 10 grupong na-sample mula sa weighted distribution. Ginagawa ng susunod na step ang mga set na ito bilang ensemble ng mga qDRIFT circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Build the qDRIFT circuits (C++) {#step-2-build-the-qdrift-circuits-c}"
msgstr "Step 2: Buuin ang mga qDRIFT circuit (C++) {#step-2-build-the-qdrift-circuits-c}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the C++ version, this step builds the circuits from the sampled operator sets. Transpilation for the target backend happens in Step 3, immediately before each circuit is submitted.\n"
msgstr "Sa C++ na bersyon, binubuo ng step na ito ang mga circuit mula sa mga na-sample na operator set. Ang transpilation para sa target na backend ay nangyayari sa Step 3, bago isumite ang bawat circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The complete program then prints circuit statistics and the operator indices of circuit 0, which are omitted here.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos, nagpi-print ang kumpletong program ng mga circuit statistic at ng mga operator index ng circuit 0, na hindi isinama rito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each sampled operator, creates a Suzuki-Trotter evolution circuit with time $t_k = \\frac{\\lambda \\tau}{n}$, where $n$ is the number of operators sampled per circuit and $\\tau$ is the time step. Because each sampled group was normalized term-by-term before mapping, this evolution applies only the phase/sign of each term during the rotation; the magnitudes contribute through the sampling distribution only. The Hartree-Fock initial state is prepared by applying X gates to qubits 0-6 and 10-16 (seven electrons in each spin sector). Each evolution circuit's instructions are manually appended to the main circuit using the C++ API.\n"
msgstr "Para sa bawat na-sample na operator, gumagawa ng Suzuki-Trotter evolution circuit na may time na $t_k = \\frac{\\lambda \\tau}{n}$, kung saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng operator na na-sample bawat circuit at ang $\\tau$ ay ang time step. Dahil ang bawat na-sample na grupo ay na-normalize term-by-term bago ang mapping, ang evolution na ito ay naglalapat lang ng phase/sign ng bawat term sa rotation; ang mga magnitude ay nag-aambag lamang sa pamamagitan ng sampling distribution. Inihahanda ang Hartree-Fock initial state sa pamamagitan ng paglalapat ng X gate sa mga qubit 0-6 at 10-16 (pitong electron sa bawat spin sector). Ang mga instruction ng bawat evolution circuit ay mano-manong idinadagdag sa pangunahing circuit gamit ang C++ API.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives (C++) {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-c}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Isagawa gamit ang Qiskit primitives (C++) {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-c}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connects to IBM Quantum, selects the backend by name, transpiles each circuit for that backend, and submits **one job per circuit**: 100 separate Sampler jobs of 100 shots each on a 20-qubit register. It then polls each job until it finishes and collects the bitstrings from `result[0]`. Every job uses QPU time and waits in the queue separately, so expect this step to take much longer than a single batched job.\n"
msgstr "Kumokonekta sa IBM Quantum, pinipili ang backend ayon sa pangalan, tina-transpile ang bawat circuit para sa backend na iyon, at nagsusumite ng **isang job bawat circuit**: 100 hiwalay na Sampler job na may tig-100 shot sa isang 20-qubit register. Pagkatapos, pino-poll nito ang bawat job hanggang matapos at kinokolekta ang mga bitstring mula sa `result[0]`. Gumagamit ng QPU time ang bawat job at hiwalay na naghihintay sa queue, kaya asahan na mas matagal ang step na ito kaysa sa iisang batched na job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware results quoted on this page come from a run on `ibm_pittsburgh` (100 circuits × 100 shots), with `backend_name` changed from the default `ibm_fez`. The saved samples were postprocessed with the corrected determinant bit ordering shown in Step 4. Hardware noise varies between runs, so your counts and final energy will differ.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga resulta ng hardware na sinipi sa pahinang ito ay galing sa takbo sa `ibm_pittsburgh` (100 circuit × 100 shot), na ang `backend_name` ay pinalitan mula sa default na `ibm_fez`. Ang mga na-save na sample ay pinoproseso gamit ang naitamang determinant bit ordering na ipinakita sa Step 4. Nag-iiba ang ingay ng hardware sa bawat takbo, kaya iba ang iyong mga bilang at final energy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Changing the backend:** Change `backend_name` in `SqDRIFT.cpp` to target a different device; `service.backends()` lists what your account can reach.\n"
msgstr "**Pagpapalit ng backend:** Palitan ang `backend_name` sa `SqDRIFT.cpp` para i-target ang ibang device; inililista ng `service.backends()` ang maaabot ng account mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format (C++) {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format-c}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical format (C++) {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format-c}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Postselect bitstrings and write CI strings {#postselect-bitstrings-and-write-ci-strings}"
msgstr "I-postselect ang mga bitstring at isulat ang mga CI string {#postselect-bitstrings-and-write-ci-strings}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Postselects bitstrings with the correct Hamming weight (n_alpha spin-up, n_beta spin-down electrons, derived from the FCIDump `NELEC` field), converts them to Configuration Interaction (CI) strings using spin symmetrization, and writes them to `alphadets_from_sqd.txt` for subsequent Selected Basis Diagonalization.\n"
msgstr "Nagpo-postselect ng mga bitstring na may tamang Hamming weight (n_alpha spin-up, n_beta spin-down na electron, hango sa field na `NELEC` ng FCIDump), kino-convert ang mga ito sa Configuration Interaction (CI) string gamit ang spin symmetrization, at isinusulat ang mga ito sa `alphadets_from_sqd.txt` para sa susunod na Selected Basis Diagonalization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clean up resources {#clean-up-resources}"
msgstr "Linisin ang mga resource {#clean-up-resources}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
