msgid "How this differs from the Python example {#how-this-differs-from-the-python-example}"
msgstr "Paano ito naiiba sa Python example {#how-this-differs-from-the-python-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two examples differ in several respects at once, not only in how they treat bad-symmetry bitstrings, so they are not expected to produce identical energies:\n"
msgstr "Magkaiba ang dalawang example sa ilang aspeto nang sabay-sabay, hindi lang sa kung paano nila tinatrato ang mga bitstring na may maling symmetry, kaya hindi inaasahang magbibigay sila ng magkaparehong energy:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | C++ tab | Python tab |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Bad-symmetry bitstrings | **Discarded** by `postselect_bitstrings` on Hamming weight | **Repaired** by iterative configuration recovery |\n"
"| Loop structure | Single pass: sample → postselect → diagonalize once | Outer loop: diagonalize, read orbital occupancies, recover configurations, re-diagonalize |\n"
"| Circuit count | 100 circuits (`num_circuits = 100`) | 400 circuits (200 per evolution time) |\n"
"| Evolution times | A single $\\tau$ (`time_step = 1`) | Two times, `times = [1.0, 10.0]` |\n"
"| Diagonal terms | Kept in the sampled operator | Removed by `filter_diagonal_terms`, changing the sampling distribution and the circuits |\n"
"| Term ordering | Grouped only | `canonical_order` applied before grouping for reproducibility |\n"
"| Diagonalization solver | **SBD** (`diag`, external MPI/OpenMP binary) | `qiskit-addon-sqd` in-process solver |\n"
"| Backend | Fixed by name (`backend_name = \"ibm_fez\"`; the run on this page used `ibm_pittsburgh`) | `least_busy` operational backend with enough qubits |\n"
"| Transpilation | Each circuit separately, optimization level 2 | All circuits together, optimization level 3 |\n"
"| Job submission | 100 jobs, one circuit each | One Sampler job containing all 400 circuits |\n"
"| Simulator run | None; hardware only | Noiseless simulator example before the hardware run |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | C++ tab | Python tab |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Mga bitstring na may maling symmetry | **Itinatapon** ng `postselect_bitstrings` ayon sa Hamming weight | **Inaayos** ng iterative configuration recovery |\n"
"| Istruktura ng loop | Isang pass: sample → postselect → diagonalize nang isang beses | Outer loop: diagonalize, basahin ang orbital occupancies, i-recover ang mga configuration, i-diagonalize ulit |\n"
"| Bilang ng circuit | 100 circuit (`num_circuits = 100`) | 400 circuit (200 bawat evolution time) |\n"
"| Mga evolution time | Isang $\\tau$ (`time_step = 1`) | Dalawang time, `times = [1.0, 10.0]` |\n"
"| Mga diagonal term | Pinapanatili sa na-sample na operator | Inaalis ng `filter_diagonal_terms`, na nagbabago sa sampling distribution at sa mga circuit |\n"
"| Pagkakasunod ng term | Naka-group lang | Inilalapat ang `canonical_order` bago mag-group para sa reproducibility |\n"
"| Diagonalization solver | **SBD** (`diag`, external na MPI/OpenMP binary) | In-process na solver ng `qiskit-addon-sqd` |\n"
"| Backend | Nakatakda ayon sa pangalan (`backend_name = \"ibm_fez\"`; ang takbo sa pahinang ito ay gumamit ng `ibm_pittsburgh`) | `least_busy` na operational backend na may sapat na qubit |\n"
"| Transpilation | Bawat circuit nang hiwalay, optimization level 2 | Lahat ng circuit nang sabay-sabay, optimization level 3 |\n"
"| Pagsusumite ng job | 100 job, isang circuit bawat isa | Isang Sampler job na naglalaman ng lahat ng 400 circuit |\n"
"| Simulator run | Wala; hardware lang | Noiseless na simulator example bago ang hardware run |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both versions use the same Hamiltonian, group its terms by electronic structure, weight each group by the mean absolute coefficient of its terms, start from the Hartree-Fock state, and sample 10 groups and 100 shots per circuit.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang dalawang bersyon ng parehong Hamiltonian, ginagrupo ang mga term nito ayon sa electronic structure, tinitimbang ang bawat grupo ayon sa mean absolute coefficient ng mga term nito, nagsisimula sa Hartree-Fock state, at nagsa-sample ng 10 grupo at 100 shot bawat circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each difference affects the sampled subspace, and therefore the energy, independently. The larger ensemble and the second, longer evolution time both broaden the configurations the Python example explores; sampling at more than one time gives SqDRIFT its Krylov-like coverage of the low-energy space. Filtering diagonal terms changes which operators the sampler can draw and their weights, so the two runs sample different distributions.\n"
msgstr "Bawat pagkakaiba ay nakakaapekto sa na-sample na subspace, at kaya sa energy, nang nakapag-iisa. Parehong pinalalawak ng mas malaking ensemble at ng pangalawa, mas mahabang evolution time ang mga configuration na ine-explore ng Python example; ang pagsa-sample sa higit sa isang time ang nagbibigay sa SqDRIFT ng Krylov-like na saklaw ng low-energy space. Binabago ng pag-filter ng mga diagonal term kung aling mga operator ang maaaring kunin ng sampler at ang kanilang mga weight, kaya magkaibang distribution ang sina-sample ng dalawang takbo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Postselection is a strict filter, and a shot with the wrong particle number is dropped outright. In the run above that discarded most of the data, 1137 of 10000 shots survived the (7,7) Hamming-weight check (about 11%), collapsing into just 49 distinct $\\alpha$-determinants. Configuration recovery instead uses average orbital occupancies from a prior diagonalization to flip bits and *repair* such shots, recycling what postselection would discard. That feedback makes it inherently iterative: `recover_configurations` in `qiskit-addon-sqd-hpc` requires an `avg_occupancies` argument that exists only after a diagonalization has run.\n"
msgstr "Mahigpit na filter ang postselection, at ang shot na may maling particle number ay tuluyang itinatapon. Sa takbo sa itaas, nagtapon ito ng karamihan sa data: 1137 sa 10000 shot ang pumasa sa (7,7) Hamming-weight check (mga 11%), na nauwi sa 49 lang na natatanging $\\alpha$-determinant. Sa halip, ginagamit ng configuration recovery ang average orbital occupancies mula sa naunang diagonalization para i-flip ang mga bit at *ayusin* ang mga ganoong shot, na nire-recycle ang itatapon sana ng postselection. Dahil sa feedback na iyon, likas itong iterative: ang `recover_configurations` sa `qiskit-addon-sqd-hpc` ay nangangailangan ng argumentong `avg_occupancies` na umiiral lamang pagkatapos tumakbo ang isang diagonalization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This C++ run yields a subspace of 49 $\\alpha$-determinants and an energy of `-107.5109` Ha. The full $\\alpha$-determinant space for seven electrons in 10 orbitals is only $\\binom{10}{7} = 120$ strings, so feeding all 120 to the same `diag` binary gives the exact FCI energy `-107.6482` Ha. The run therefore sits about `0.1373` Ha above exact while spanning 49 of the 120 $\\alpha$-determinants. Since SQD is variational in the selected subspace, a smaller subspace can only raise the energy, so the incomplete subspace is the most direct reading of the gap.\n"
msgstr "Ang C++ run na ito ay nagbibigay ng subspace na 49 $\\alpha$-determinant at energy na `-107.5109` Ha. Ang buong $\\alpha$-determinant space para sa pitong electron sa 10 orbital ay $\\binom{10}{7} = 120$ string lang, kaya ang pagpapasok ng lahat ng 120 sa parehong `diag` binary ay nagbibigay ng eksaktong FCI energy na `-107.6482` Ha. Kaya ang takbo ay nasa humigit-kumulang `0.1373` Ha sa itaas ng eksakto habang sumasaklaw sa 49 sa 120 $\\alpha$-determinant. Dahil variational ang SQD sa napiling subspace, ang mas maliit na subspace ay maaari lang magpataas ng energy, kaya ang hindi kumpletong subspace ang pinakadirektang paliwanag sa agwat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This exact-FCI check is only possible because the example is small; it is not part of the SqDRIFT workflow, and for system sizes where SQD is actually needed, no such reference exists. It serves here only to quantify how much of the space this run recovered.\n"
msgstr "Posible lang ang exact-FCI check na ito dahil maliit ang example; hindi ito bahagi ng SqDRIFT workflow, at para sa mga laki ng sistema kung saan talagang kailangan ang SQD, walang ganoong reference. Nagsisilbi lang itong sukatin kung gaano karami ng space ang nabawi ng takbong ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A comparison against the Python example is not controlled, so a difference should not be attributed to the absence of configuration recovery alone; note that circuit count, the single evolution time, diagonal-term filtering, and hardware noise all differ at once and all shape the subspace.\n"
msgstr "Hindi kontrolado ang paghahambing sa Python example, kaya hindi dapat iugnay ang pagkakaiba sa kawalan lang ng configuration recovery; tandaan na magkakaiba nang sabay-sabay ang bilang ng circuit, ang iisang evolution time, ang diagonal-term filtering, at ang ingay ng hardware, at lahat ay humuhubog sa subspace.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To close the gap, here are some possible next steps to try after completing this tutorial: raise `shots`, `num_circuits`, or `ops_per_circuit`; sample at more than one `time_step`; and add a recovery loop on top of `Qiskit::addon::sqd::recover_configurations`.\n"
msgstr "Para mapaliit ang agwat, narito ang ilang posibleng susunod na hakbang na subukan pagkatapos makumpleto ang tutorial na ito: dagdagan ang `shots`, `num_circuits`, o `ops_per_circuit`; mag-sample sa higit sa isang `time_step`; at magdagdag ng recovery loop sa ibabaw ng `Qiskit::addon::sqd::recover_configurations`.\n"

